            <ArticleTitle>[To surpass coronary luminology with interventional physiology].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>41-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Interventional physiology, as much as anatomic parameters, ultimately determine the functional status and well being of a patient. Although technical improvements in equipment and more clinical studies are needed, the current experience indicates that interventional physiology has moved from a research tool to clinical adjunct. A physiologic approach complements coronary interventions and has important clinical and economic implications for patients undergoing invasive treatment of coronary artery disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
